From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DroidDeck <droiddeck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] stats: count the tracer's stops in a file another process can
 read at any moment

With PROOT_STATS=<file> (and only then), the tracer creates that file, maps
it MAP_SHARED and keeps in it, as it goes: every stop by kind (seccomp entry,
PTRACE_SYSCALL entry and exit, SIGSYS, clone/fork/vfork/exec/exit events,
signals, exits) with the CLOCK_MONOTONIC time spent handling them, and, per
syscall, the entries, exits and refused-syscall emulations it handled with
their time. A reader takes a snapshot whenever it likes: no signal, no syscall
on the tracer's side, nothing to flush. Without PROOT_STATS a stop costs one
test of a null pointer; translate_syscall() and the SIGSYS handler only store
what they already know.
---
